course: dictionary
lesson: 1109
title: Bravely and how actions are described
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words tell us how something is done. Bravely is one of them. It comes from the word brave, and the ending -ly turns it into a word that tells us how an action happens. «The girl bravely climbed the rope to the top of the tree.» We know she climbed, and bravely tells us how: without showing fear.
explain: Bravely does not only mean a fight or a storm. You can also be brave when something is hard or sad. «She smiled bravely when the doctor gave her an injection.» Her smile was not a big happy one. She smiled to show she was trying hard, even though it was difficult.
explain: Look at the words around bravely to check its meaning. What is the action? What makes it hard? In «The Butterfly says, as bravely as he can: "Of course it doesn't make any difference to me..."», the Butterfly is trying to sound calm, even though he may be hurt or upset. The clue is as bravely as he can.
fact: Bravely is an adverb. It tells us how someone does something.
fact: Bravely comes from the adjective brave. The adverb forms are bravely, more bravely and most bravely.
fact: «Bravely» means in a brave way, without showing fear, even when something is dangerous, painful or frightening.
fact: «Bravely» can also mean trying hard, even when something is difficult or sad, as in «She smiled bravely».
fact: Useful phrases are bravely fought, smiled bravely and bravely faced. Check your meaning by swapping in "in a brave way" and seeing if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The firefighter bravely ran into the burning house.» What does bravely tell us? | In a wet and muddy way | In a slow and lazy way | In a quiet, whispering way | *In a brave way, without showing fear
exercise: Bravely comes from which adjective? | fearful | *brave | bake | bare
exercise: «The Butterfly says, as bravely as he can: "Of course it doesn't make any difference to me."» What does bravely show about the Butterfly? | He is very sleepy and wants to rest | *He is trying hard to stay calm, even though it is difficult | He has forgotten what he wanted to say | He is shouting with joy
test: «He faced the big test bravely, even though his hands were shaking.» What does bravely mean? | Very quickly | Angrily | *Without showing fear, even though it was hard | Quietly and sleepily
test: Which sentence uses bravely correctly? | The dog bravely slept all afternoon | *Mia bravely walked into the dark cave | The soup was bravely hot and tasty | The sun bravely set behind the hill
exam: Ella says bravely means loudly, like a shout. Is she right? | No, bravely means sleepily and slowly | *No, bravely means without showing fear, even when something is hard | Yes, bravely means very loudly | Yes, bravely means fast and noisy
